                        "glosses": [
                            "Characteristic of an ass or donkey."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "69d5c6c0-01de-423a-89b5-4ba413b96788",
                                "sense_id": "045c1549-9f2e-30b5-b139-9f3239667117",
                                "text": "Further, he quickly got him a beast to ride on, far, for sumptuous glory, beyond — though as to nature as assish a creature as — that on which Balaam was wont to ride; and by this exaltation he not only became more stately, but the horns of the beast would push for him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0b5e9212-bb4c-45b6-b53e-20cde96d5687",
                                "sense_id": "045c1549-9f2e-30b5-b139-9f3239667117",
                                "text": "On the 24th March, 1875, a donkey-show, which has since been continued periodically, was held in connection with Mr. Orsman's work; and on that occasion the assish celebrity COSTER, depicted in our engraving, was presented to Lord Shaftesbury by the exhibitors, amid a scene of great enthusiasm."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b08ba585-2024-4bd5-90f6-612bd0b2ab3c",
                                "sense_id": "045c1549-9f2e-30b5-b139-9f3239667117",
                                "text": "The ape, to know whether the ass's talking Were any quicker than his assish stalking, Asked the ass, \"If thou should'st choose one of both — To run as swiftly as the greyhound yonder go'th. Or turn as light as the hare — which one of twain, obtain?\""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1b517a18-140a-3e13-a476-fca486a5bc77",
                        "entry_id": "5d297c96-dfe7-3209-8edf-934749620361",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Stupid or obstinate; asinine."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f7b2a3bd-6232-4035-b723-c9b7f7e5851b",
                                "sense_id": "1b517a18-140a-3e13-a476-fca486a5bc77",
                                "text": "c. 1795, Peter Pindar (John Wolcot), Liberty's Last Squeak\nan assish, mulish, packhorse clan"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f5e45926-f6bf-4530-a867-0ec7ba4f86af",
                                "sense_id": "1b517a18-140a-3e13-a476-fca486a5bc77",
                                "text": "All taffy so far, except “Sigma,” whose lucubrations make me think of dear old Gurowski's phrase of objurgation— “Sir, you are an asinine assish ass!”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5cc83811-c426-48e1-a869-0428503eaad4",
                                "sense_id": "1b517a18-140a-3e13-a476-fca486a5bc77",
                                "text": "Yet one could easily fall into a habit of thinking Thompson a bit of an ass, amiable and solemn, but still assish."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
